Last London rgrn I suggested a change of venue, to the Oakdale Arms in NE
London. I'd like to take a straw poll here as to which pub we should go
to.

The Oakdale has a Website; http://www.individualpubs.co.uk/oakdale/ .

The Oakdale is probably harder to get to - about ten minutes walk from
either Manor House or Seven Sisters Tube stations - except for those
coming from Cambridge, who can get off at Finsbury Park and make a short
Tube journey.

The Oakdale has better beer - about half a dozen Milton beers, and typically
2 guest beers, and one proper cider on tap - and unlike the Lord Moon
these won't all be off when we arrive. :-) However it'll be more like L2 a
pint than the L1.60 for the guest ales at the Lord Moon, and I think
people who drink nasty lager will be stuck with bottles.

The Oakdale will have plenty of space.

Conversely they don't know for sure that the kitchen will be up and
running by the 29th May. They do baked potatoes, and are happy for people
to bring in food of their own.

I'm a little ambivalent; we could wait until July, when the kitchen will
definitely be operating, or chance it this month. If people say what
they'd like, I'll issue a diktat on Friday.
